## Pipeline / persistence
- Wire graph row creation: insert `Graph` (status=building) early in dispatcher; backfill `tree.graph_id` after `index_tree`
- Wire `sync_runs`: open RUNNING row at dispatch start, close SUCCESS/ERROR with counters at end (FULL + PATCH)
- PATCH flow: implement `_mcp_incremental_sync` — `git pull` + `git diff --name-status -M`, load tree from DB, run C5/C6 on changed files only, mutate tree (drop nodes/edges from changed files, re-add from re-parse, fix cross-file edges), update `trees` row
- Repo cache eviction: TTL (7d idle) + LRU disk-budget; mark `repo_clones.evicted_at`, keep row as tombstone for re-clone

## Graph layer (C8 / C9)
- C8 graph builder: NetworkX merge of EXTRACTED + INFERRED edges from `trees.tree_data`
- C9 Leiden clustering: graspologic, populate communities + god nodes + surprises
- Finalize graph: write clustered output to `graphs.graph_data`, populate `node_count` / `edge_count` / `community_count`, flip `status` to `ready`, stamp `last_synced_at` and `last_commit_sha`

## API surface
- `GET /trees/{tree_id}` — fetch indexed parse tree
- `GET /repos/{graph_id}/graph` — fetch clustered graph (post-C9)
- `DELETE /repos/{graph_id}` — explicit graph delete (cascades to trees + sync_runs)
- `WS /repos/{graph_id}/status` — stream build progress (driven by `sync_runs` updates)
- `POST /repos/{graph_id}/query` — C11 QnA (BFS subgraph + ClaudeSDKClient)

## Auth
- `/auth/register`, `/auth/login`, JWT middleware
- Scope all `/repos` and `/trees` queries by `user_id` from JWT
- Flip `tree.graph_id`, `graphs.user_id`, `repo_clones.user_id` to NOT NULL once auth lands and rows are always user-scoped

## Frontend
- C12 React frontend: react-force-graph-3d viewer, semantic zoom, served as static SPA from FastAPI

## Cleanup
- Remove `ENV=dev` fixture short-circuit in `surgical_agent/resolver.py` once C6 is exercised end-to-end
